      "note": "An absolute floor on clearance, independent of which objective is seated. It equals the tightest working distance across the six (100x Oil, MRD71970), so it never binds while the lookup above is right. It catches a looked-up limit that has come out too small: a store value below 130 um, or a missing or corrupt entry. It does not catch a clearance estimate that is itself wrong, such as one computed with the wrong objective after a mis-seated nosepiece. Both limits are minima on clearance, so the LARGER of the two binds."
